==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|einn|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*ainaz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*óynos}}. Compare Faroese and Norwegian Nynorsk {{term|ein|lang=fo}}, Danish, Swedish, and Norwegian Bokmål {{term|en|lang=da}}.

===Numeral===
'''einn''' {{g|m}}, '''[[ein]]''' {{g|f}}, '''[[eitt]]''' {{g|n}}

# '''[[one]]'''; the cardinal number after [[núll#Icelandic|núll]] and before [[tveir#Icelandic|tveir]].
# accusative masculine singular form of [[einn#Icelandic|einn]]

====Declension====
{{is-numeral (einn)|}}

